From 8fd5f37bed402b69bece887119f583df9eb3a101 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johnny Collado <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:04:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] Recompiler: `module` config builds an overlay as a
 guest module

With `module = "<name>"` in [general], the input is treated as a module loaded
at run time rather than the program: every generated function name and file
gets the prefix "<name>_" (overlays sharing an address can link into one
binary), the headers are <name>_recompiled_functions.h/_stubs.h, and instead of
the global g_ps2RecompiledFunctionTable it writes <name>_register_functions.cpp,
which fills the module's own table and registers it with
ps2RegisterGuestModule, fingerprinted by the first 64 bytes of the module's
lowest loaded section. Without `module` the output is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
